<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,260.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,260.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,260 today from 1,258 on May 1, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1358    12.331	  1343    12.192</p>
<p>   1a   1234  9344.000	  1230  9317.000</p>
<p>   2    1520    21.713	  1522    21.742</p>
<p>   2a   1467 12031.000	  1475 12100.000</p>
<p>   3    1360    12.550	  1362    12.567</p>
<p>   3a   1132  8938.000	  1124  8875.000</p>
